== 2. Streaming replica setup ==
================================================================
 ReadWell Libraries - streaming replica setup (Portfolio 5)
 Student: Nuhu Simbiat - 2026/A/MIT/0955
 Primary data dir : /var/lib/postgresql/16/main
 Replica data dir : /var/lib/postgresql/16/replica
 Replica port     : 5433
 Replication slot : replica_slot
================================================================

== STEP 1: Configure PRIMARY postgresql.conf for replication ==
   wal_level=replica, max_wal_senders=10, max_replication_slots=10,
   listen_addresses='localhost'
   backed up original -> /etc/postgresql/16/main/postgresql.conf.orig
   primary postgresql.conf updated.

== STEP 2: PREPEND replication trust lines to TOP of pg_hba.conf ==
   backed up original -> /etc/postgresql/16/main/pg_hba.conf.orig
   pg_hba.conf trust block now at the TOP of the file.

== STEP 3: Restart PostgreSQL primary ==
   primary restarted.
   live settings:
listen_addresses = localhost
max_replication_slots = 10
max_wal_senders = 10
wal_level = replica

== STEP 4: Stop any existing replica cluster on port 5433 ==
 pg_drop_replication_slot 
--------------------------
(0 rows)

   replica data dir is now empty: /var/lib/postgresql/16/replica

